## Usage

### Option 1: Docker Compose (Recommended)

Create `.env` file in `2_orchestration/`:

```bash
cp MASTER_PIPELINE_CONFIG.template .env

# Edit .env with your values
nano .env

# Docker compose automatically loads .env
docker compose up -d
```

### Option 2: Kubernetes ConfigMap

For Kubernetes deployments:

```bash
kubectl create configmap airflow-pipeline-config --from-env-file=.env -n airflow
```

### Option 3: Environment Variables

Set manually before starting:

```bash
export SQL_SERVER=DESKTOP-B0PDEI7
export SQL_PORT=1434
# ... etc
docker compose up -d
```

